// LAB VERSION of queries/05-recovery-change-from-new-ip.kql. Generated by tools/build_labs.py; do not edit.
// Synthetic data only. now() is pinned to datetime(2026-03-11T00:00:00Z).
// Title: MFA / account recovery changes from an IP the user has never signed in from
// Description: Attackers who get a session often register their own authenticator or phone
//   number so they survive a password reset. This flags security info and password changes
//   where the initiating IP has no successful sign-in for that user in the prior baseline.
// Tables: AuditLogs, SigninLogs
// MITRE: T1556.006, T1098.005
// False positives: New phone or laptop on a new home network. Users who travel. Admin-initiated
//   changes always show the admin's IP, so they'll surface unless you split them out (the
//   Actor column makes that easy).
// Tuning: Extend baseline to 30d for low-activity users. Join to the sign-in that preceded
//   the change to see the client and country.
// Expected lab results: 1 row. dana@lab.example "User registered security info" from
//   198.51.100.77. ravi@lab.example's change from his usual IP is not returned.

let SigninLogs = datatable(TimeGenerated:datetime, UserPrincipalName:string, IPAddress:string, ResultType:string, ResultDescription:string, AppDisplayName:string, UserAgent:string, LocationDetails:dynamic) [
    datetime(2026-03-01T15:10:00Z), "dana@lab.example", "203.0.113.10", "0", "", "Office 365 Exchange Online", "Microsoft Office/16.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Microsoft Outlook 16.0)", dynamic({"countryOrRegion":"US","city":"Houston"}),
